        "hypothesis_kind": "explanatory",
        "hypothesis_status": "proposed",
        "statement": "Since the activation energy is constant with Cu/Zn, a premise is possible that all active centres are alike and appear more frequently on the surface with increasing copper content; the authors expect a steep rise of the frequency factor per unit area with decreasing Cu/Zn at extremely low ratios (toward the higher values of zinc oxide-chromium oxide catalysts), for which no data are yet available."
      }
